================================================================
 rmnet UL csum offload — NETIF_F_IP_CSUM features flag
================================================================

 Tiny addition to upstream mainline rmnet's rmnet_vnd.c:

   rmnet_dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM;
   rmnet_dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_GRO_HW;     (vendor parity)
   rmnet_dev->features    |= NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM;

 Without this, when EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV4 (UL QMAPv3) is enabled via
 the qmapv3_ul_enable module param, the kernel network stack uses
 orig_dev->features to decide whether to skip software csum, falls
 back to memset-zero of the UL csum header → modem gets UL frames
 with zeroed csum metadata → drops.

 Applies on top of upstream mainline rmnet (drivers/net/ethernet/
 qualcomm/rmnet/). Standalone from the IPA driver port — small
 feature-flag patch that could be a single upstreamable commit.

================================================================

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_vnd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/rmnet/rmnet_vnd.c
@@ -312,7 +312,23 @@
 	}
 
 	rmnet_dev->hw_features = NETIF_F_RXCSUM;
+	rmnet_dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM;
 	rmnet_dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_SG;
+	/* Vendor 4.19 parity (rmnet_vnd.c:373): tell net stack the underlying
+	 * IPA HW can do GRO coalescing. Without this, kernel skips GRO opportunities
+	 * for adjacent in-order TCP segments → higher per-packet overhead → cwnd
+	 * ramping slower. Comprehensive audit 2026-05-30 Finding A. */
+	rmnet_dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
+
+	/* 2026-05-31 fix for UL QMAPv3: rmnet_map_v4_checksum_uplink_packet
+	 * checks orig_dev->features for NETIF_F_IP_CSUM/IPV6_CSUM and falls
+	 * back to memset-zero of the UL csum header if neither is enabled
+	 * (only hw_features was set). With EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV4 flag on, this
+	 * causes modem to receive UL frames with zeroed csum metadata → drops.
+	 * Enable the csum offload features by default so mainline rmnet can
+	 * fill the UL csum header properly when the flag is set. */
+	rmnet_dev->features |= NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM;
+
 	priv->real_dev = real_dev;
 
 	headroom = rmnet_vnd_headroom(port);
